{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-2","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-2","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.md","line":84,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.tex#def:dc-ch6-2-2","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-2-locality]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#prop:dc-ch6-2-1]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-3-normal-connection]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-3-weingarten]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions.tex","label":"def:dc-ch6-2-2","line":213,"source":"\\begin{definition}[second fundamental form $\\mathit{II}_\\eta$]\n  \\label{def:dc-ch6-2-2}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch6-2-locality, prop:dc-ch6-2-1, def:dc-ch6-3-normal-connection, lem:dc-ch6-3-weingarten}\n\n  \\dcref{ch6:2.2}\n  The quadratic form $\\mathit{II}_\\eta$ defined on $T_pM$ by\n  $$\n  \\mathit{II}_\\eta(x)=H_\\eta(x,x)\n  $$\n  is called \\emph{the second fundamental form} of $f$ at $p$ along the normal vector\n  $\\eta$. Sometimes the expression \\emph{second fundamental form} also designates the\n  mapping $B$. The bilinear mapping $H_\\eta$ is associated to a linear self-adjoint\n  operator $S_\\eta:T_pM\\to T_pM$ by\n  $$\n  \\langle S_\\eta(x),y\\rangle=H_\\eta(x,y)=\\langle B(x,y),\\eta\\rangle.\n  $$\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[second fundamental form <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathit{II}_\\eta $\">$\\mathit{II}_\\eta $</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a64632d6368362d322d32\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23lem%3Adc-ch6-2-locality\">↗ lem:dc-ch6-2-locality</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23prop%3Adc-ch6-2-1\">↗ prop:dc-ch6-2-1</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23def%3Adc-ch6-3-normal-connection\">↗ def:dc-ch6-3-normal-connection</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_IsometricImmersions%23lem%3Adc-ch6-3-weingarten\">↗ lem:dc-ch6-3-weingarten</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch6:2.2</span></span>The quadratic form <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathit{II}_\\eta $\">$\\mathit{II}_\\eta $</span> defined on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM$\">$T_pM$</span> by <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\mathit{II}_\\eta (x)=H_\\eta (x,x)  \\]\">\\[  \\mathit{II}_\\eta (x)=H_\\eta (x,x)  \\]</span> is called <em>the second fundamental form</em> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> along the normal vector <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\eta $\">$\\eta $</span>. Sometimes the expression <em>second fundamental form</em> also designates the mapping <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B$\">$B$</span>. The bilinear mapping <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H_\\eta $\">$H_\\eta $</span> is associated to a linear self-adjoint operator <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S_\\eta :T_pM\\to T_pM$\">$S_\\eta :T_pM\\to T_pM$</span> by <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\langle S_\\eta (x),y\\rangle =H_\\eta (x,y)=\\langle B(x,y),\\eta \\rangle .  \\]\">\\[  \\langle S_\\eta (x),y\\rangle =H_\\eta (x,y)=\\langle B(x,y),\\eta \\rangle .  \\]</span> ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-2-locality","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#prop:dc-ch6-2-3","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-2-locality","title":"lem:dc-ch6-2-locality","label":"lem:dc-ch6-2-locality"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#prop:dc-ch6-2-1","title":"prop:dc-ch6-2-1","label":"prop:dc-ch6-2-1"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-3-normal-connection","title":"def:dc-ch6-3-normal-connection","label":"def:dc-ch6-3-normal-connection"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-3-weingarten","title":"lem:dc-ch6-3-weingarten","label":"lem:dc-ch6-3-weingarten"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#prop:dc-ch6-2-3","title":"prop:dc-ch6-2-3","label":"prop:dc-ch6-2-3"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#ex:dc-ch6-2-4","title":"ex:dc-ch6-2-4","label":"ex:dc-ch6-2-4"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal","title":"def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal","label":"def:dc-ch6-2-4-principal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#lem:dc-ch6-2-7-gauss-form","title":"lem:dc-ch6-2-7-gauss-form","label":"lem:dc-ch6-2-7-gauss-form"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_IsometricImmersions#ex: